WEBVTT

00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:15,360
Plant cannabinoids like THC and CBD are a special class of compounds derived from cannabis,

00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:18,480
which interact with our body's endocannabinoid system.

00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,960
The network of cellular receptors in the body that helps us maintain homeostasis or

00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,960
balance.

00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:28,960
One key element of the endocannabinoid system are CB1 receptors, which are located mostly

00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,960
in the brain and nervous system.

00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:36,000
These are the receptors that THC activates to produce the high associated with cannabis.

00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Unlike THC, CBD doesn't fit into CB1 receptors in the same way.

00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:47,000
For starters, this makes CBD non-intoxicating, but also gets in the way of compounds like THC,

00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
preventing them from activating CB1 receptors.

00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,840
This is why CBD can decrease some of THC's major side effects, and why balanced strains containing

00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:00,840
both THC and CBD will make you feel very different from THC dominant strains.

